This product uses the TMDB API (optional, user-supplied key) but is not
endorsed or certified by TMDB.

TV metadata is provided by TheTVDB (optional, user-supplied key),
https://thetvdb.com. Please consider adding missing information or subscribing.

Games are played through libretro cores and, optionally, a RetroArch-based
runner. These are separate programs with their own licences (some GPL), are not
part of WittyMediaServer, and run only as separate processes. None is bundled
unless a release says so. No game or BIOS files are bundled, downloaded or linked.

A person's own gaming PC can be played through Sunshine and Moonlight, which are
separate GPL-3.0 projects, installed separately, and not part of WittyMediaServer.
This product only talks to them over the network or starts them as other programs.
Browser play is moonlight-web-stream (GPL-3.0-or-later), downloaded on an admin's
request from its own project and run as a separate program. None of these is bundled.

The DVD-Video engine is WittyDVD (https://github.com/wittywilla/WittyDVD),
developed by WittyWilla as part of the WittyMediaServer project.
